                "text": "Analyse the transformation rule:\nIn all training examples:\nThere is a rectangular frame made of color 5 (gray).\nInside the frame of 5s, the contents are changed:\nNotice the two colors besides 0 in each example:\nExample 1: colors 3 and 4 (and 0).\nIn the interior:\nRow 2: `4, 5, 3, 0, 4, 0, 3, 4, 5, 3` -> interior `3, 0, 4, 0, 3, 4` became `4, 0, 3, 0, 4, 3`.\nNotice: every 3 became 4, every 4 became 3! 0 stayed 0!\nExample 2: colors 1 and 8.\nIn the interior: 1 and 8 are swapped! (1 becomes 8, 8 becomes 1, 0 stays 0).\nExample 3: colors 2 and 4.\nIn the interior: 2 and 4 are swapped!\nExample 4: colors 6 and 7.\nIn the interior: 6 and 7 are swapped!\nExample 5: colors 1 and 3.\nIn the interior: 1 and 3 are swapped!\n\nSo the rule is:\n1. Find the bounding box / frame formed by 5s.\n2. Inside this frame (strictly between the top/bottom and left/right boundaries of the 5s frame), swap the two non-zero, non-5 foreground colors. Everything else remains unchanged.\n\nReady for the test input. Please provide the test input grid.",
